        ["NativeFrames.Title"] = "Window styling",
        ["NativeFrames.Heading"] = "One frame. All around.",
        ["NativeFrames.Description"] = "Optional: flush live-glass title bars and left-hand window buttons for eligible 32-/64-bit windows, including WPF with standard frames. Experimental Explorer, Paint and Notepad adapters require additional approval. Other app-drawn title bars remain protected.",
        ["NativeFrames.Manage"] = "Manage window styling",
        ["NativeFrames.Enable"] = "Automatically style compatible apps",
        ["NativeFrames.Consent"] = "Enable automatic window styling?\n\nVeliShell may load its matching native DLL into eligible classic 32-/64-bit apps in your session, including WPF with standard frames and apps started later. Title, sides, bottom edge and corners use the shared glass frame. No global hooks, system file changes or administrator rights.\n\nExperimental: save your work. Add games, anti-cheat-protected and critical apps to exceptions first. App-drawn title bars are never covered; limited native appearance adjustments require a separate opt-in. Protected and elevated windows stay unchanged.\n\nEmergency: Ctrl + Alt + Shift + F12 or WINDOW-RECOVERY.cmd. Hung apps must respond again for recovery to finish. After rollback the DLL stays loaded but inactive until you close that app. Continue?",
